    "summary": "High‑energy Spectrum show with epic Dark Star→Morning Dew and tight jams",
    "blurb": "Features a blistering Dark Star > Morning Dew sandwich, soaring Bird Song and a crisp first‑set run through classics like Cumberland Blues and Playing In The Band. Jerry’s guitar is in peak form while Phil’s bass anchors the extended improvisations. Soundboard recordings are crystal clear, making this one of the most listenable 1972 shows.",
    "review": "The Spectrum on September 21 1972 delivers a night that still feels electric decades later. From the opening \"The Promised Land\" through a tight first set that rolls from Bird Song into El Paso and a flawless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, the band builds a solid groove that erupts in the second set. A 35‑minute Dark Star blossoms into an inspired Morning Dew, with Jerry’s wailing leads and Keith’s jazzy piano paints a vivid canvas while Bill Kreutzmann powers the marathon with relentless drive. Highlights continue with He's Gone → Truckin', a fiery Playing In The Band, and a soaring Sugar Magnolia that caps a set packed with high‑octane energy. The soundboard sources (Masse and Miller mixes) capture every nuance – crisp instrument separation, balanced mix, and just enough room ambience to make you feel right in the audience. For anyone hunting an essential 1972 performance, this Spectrum show is both historically significant and sonically superb.",
